<title>MEXICO: Far-Ben says to offer convertible bonds.</title>
<headline>Far-Ben says to offer convertible bonds.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican pharmacy company, Far-Ben SA de CV will make a public offering of 2.25 million convertible bonds, denominated in UDIs, inflation tied investment instruments, the company said in notices published in various newspapers on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bonds will be convertible for series &quot;B&quot; shares.</p>
<p>The instruments will mature on June 13, 2002.</p>
<p>The issue will be led by Bancomer, it said.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
